{"id":"agents-root","ord":"a0","title":"Agents","desc":"Who can be dispatched, one node per agent.\n\n- **Launch command:** the `command` property is THE EXACT LAUNCH COMMAND — a launcher reads it and runs it verbatim.\n  - A missing node, or a node without `command`, REFUSES the spawn loudly; nobody falls back to a machine default.\n  - Reason: the Fable burn, 2026-08-13, is why this file exists.\n- **Role:** `role` says what the agent is for.\n  - `prop:role=reviewer` lists the review bench.\n  - `prop:role=author` lists who can hold a lane.\n- **Split:** the note keeps the story and the quirks; the properties keep the facts.\n- **Spawn shape:** `kolu create --repo <repo> --worktree <branch> --json -- <command>`\n- When kolu grows a structured launch spec, these properties migrate into it.","changed":"2026-08-23T12:17:15-04:00","custom":{"merge-gate":"RULED by the human 2026-08-23 12:18, after the orchestrator merged #352 on a misread approval: NO PR IS MERGED WITHOUT THE HUMAN'S EXPLICIT APPROVAL OF THAT PR, given after its pipeline is complete (reviews folded, CI green, evidence verified) and the finished PR has been fielded to them. 'Auto-merge on verification' dispositions are void from now; 'approve' said mid-pipeline is not a merge gate. The orchestrator fields, the human merges — or says 'merge'."}}
{"id":"agent-claude-opus","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a0","title":"claude-opus — the author agent","desc":"Claude Code pinned to Opus with the 1M context window (`opus[1m]`), YOLO mode. The default author for dispatched lanes. Verify with the banner: it must say Opus, not the machine default. The `[1m]` suffix is the human's ruling of 2026-08-21 — a lane that runs for hours must not compact itself into amnesia.","changed":"2026-08-21T21:52:55-04:00","custom":{"command":"claude --model opus[1m] --dangerously-skip-permissions","context":"1M — the [1m] suffix, ruled by the human 2026-08-21 (on the Anthropic API Opus 5 is 1M natively; the suffix pins it everywhere and is harmless where it is the default)","role":"author"}}
{"id":"agent-grok","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a1","title":"grok — reviewer","desc":"Grok CLI in always-approve mode.\n\n- Reviews in a split terminal of the author's worktree.\n- Posts one review comment via gh.\n- Never edits, pushes, or merges.\n- **Authoring track record:**\n  - Shipped #64 (home-manager module) and #153 (parallel e2e) as author.\n  - 2026-08-16: its quiet-outline UI authoring attempt was judged bad by the human and discarded wholesale (terminal killed, no commits worth keeping).\n  - **Guidance:** prefer Opus for UI/design-heavy authoring, grok for reviews and infra-shaped authoring.","changed":"2026-08-22T09:38:57-04:00","custom":{"command":"grok --always-approve","role":"reviewer","usage-limit":"2026-08-22 09:40 — the status bar showed 'Weekly limit left: 8%'; the human: 'Don't worry about Grok; I can increase limit' — do NOT re-dispatch grok lanes on a low-limit reading; if a grok session actually dies on the limit, tell the human and wait"}}
{"id":"agent-opencode","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a2","title":"opencode — reviewer","desc":"opencode TUI on its configured model (kimi-k3 via Juspay at last sighting — the config is opencode's own, not spelled here).\n\n- Same reviewer contract as grok.\n- **Quirks:**\n  - Has mislabeled itself \"codex\" in a posted review once; brief it to title reviews with its tool name.\n  - On PR #193 (2026-08-15) its review asserted \"nothing else in docs//website/ enumerates chat rows or _meta fields, so no drift\" — wrong on both counts (grok found both).\n  - Weigh its no-drift claims accordingly.","changed":"2026-08-23T10:49:01-04:00","custom":{"availability":"DEAD 2026-08-23 10:47 (the human): the litellm/kimi-k3 key behind it rate-limits ('Rate limit exceeded for api_key … retrying'); reviews go to grok until the human says otherwise","command":"opencode","role":"reviewer"}}
{"id":"agent-claude-fable","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a3","title":"claude-fable — design-grade author","desc":"Claude Code pinned to Fable (the Mythos-tier model above Opus), YOLO mode. Added 2026-08-19 on the human's word, for design-first work (first use: the vault-in-browser design doc).\n- Reserve for work needing that level — it is the expensive tier; Opus stays the default author.\n- Verify with the banner: it must say Fable, not the machine default.","created":"2026-08-19T20:04:37-04:00","custom":{"command":"claude --model fable --dangerously-skip-permissions","role":"author"}}
{"id":"supervision-watcher","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a4","title":"Supervision: the watcher and the mute list","desc":"The wake mechanism (per instructions.md): `kolu watch --states waiting,awaiting --held-for 60s --nag 10m --ignore-self --heartbeat 30m` run under the harness's Monitor tool with `persistent: true` (a background Bash task notifies only on exit — a watch stream never exits; RCA 2026-08-21).\n\nThe mute list, as `--ignore` flags — fail-open (a stale id costs nothing; every NEW terminal still rings), which is what keeps it legal under the never-an-id-list doctrine. Muted 2026-08-21, all explicitly dispositioned as the HUMAN's own sessions: 0cdc41be + a5e17829 + ab047416 (the kolu#2194 handover — the human took that lane over with their own Claude; orchestrator stands down until handed back), aa15d349 (kolu·damn-spring), 3d01a0b3 (merged docs-PR session), 7251ff2b (nixos-config), 1ef72cfc (olai·master chat session), 2080355a. A terminal handed back to the orchestrator is unmuted by re-arming without its flag; a new human session that starts nagging gets muted the same way after its disposition is verified — never on assumption (identify via kolu ls first).\n\nNag discipline (RCA-2, 2026-08-21): a nag on an unchanged block is re-DERIVED, not re-acknowledged — the second nag with no new information means the block is suspect: act on standing authority or escalate it as a standalone question. A dismissal applies to an event, never to a terminal.","created":"2026-08-21T17:30:28-04:00","changed":"2026-08-24T15:40:27-04:00","custom":{"deploy-2026-08-21":"DEPLOYED ~21:20 and then the orchestrator's own process restarted ~21:25 — the watch died loudly both times as designed and was re-armed (bhb2ugljn); the SECOND restart recycled all terminal ids (the kolu skill's warning made real): the A/B experiment terminal died, every lane's terminal prop went stale, the mute list was rewritten. Production kolu now carries #2194; full real-agent verification run 21:28 (test terminal c01109d6).","kolu-ci-fleet-2026-08-22":"ABANDONED 10:41 — Incus unstable: boxes created Ready at 10:00-10:03 were gone from `pu list` (ERR instance not found) within ~30 min, ci-2 mid-e2e; kolu-ci-8 created 10:38 by me (on linux-08) and left unused; kolu-ci-3 (linux-14) still alive but out of use by ruling","kolu-ci-fleet-gist":"https://gist.github.com/srid/143288f346ba71e27cfb54e67173e3b0 — the pu create failures of 2026-08-22 in full (timeline, outputs, raw server transcripts, registry state, questions for the pu owner)","kolu-pr-process":"RULED by the human 2026-08-22 16:15: kolu PRs are taken through KOLU's own process — the author runs kolu's /be skill (.agents/skills/be/SKILL.md in the kolu checkout) instead of our review/refactor round, and CI through kolu's /ci skill (.agents/skills/ci/SKILL.md) instead of our odu recipe; both platforms green before merge; the orchestrator merges on /be done + /ci green. 16:20: the darwin host /ci names (sincereintent) has been REPLACED by ci@petit (--host aarch64-darwin=ci@petit, under /tmp/olai-odu-petit.lock). Olai PRs keep our process. First applied to lane-scli PR 1 (surface-cli-kolu).","mute-list":"RE-CONFIRMED by the human 2026-08-23 ~17:15 (question tool, mcp-roster-visible session). Human's own, never supervised: 30f81ddc 🔥 (olai master claude), d7543299 🏠 (olai master claude), 724a754e (nixos-config grok) + splits a5d75521/f6331d54, bd0a0a9d (kolu-surface-cli opencode) + splits 418a9061/8d5c8b80, 2960c89a agent-debate:pi-2208-claude (kolu #2208, driven by its own harness — never submit its staged prompts). Generalized (orchestrator, the human may overrule): a terminal no lane's `terminal` prop names, outside olai's worktrees, is presumed the human's — nags are no-ops. Mine this session: 2a38138b = lane-mrv author (claude-opus). Ids rotate on kaval restart — re-identify by intent.","odu-venue":"RULING 10:50 2026-08-22 (human): kolu-ci-* dead. TWO venues in parallel, each one-run-at-a-time under a local flock: localhost x86_64-linux (/tmp/olai-odu-localhost.lock, --host x86_64-linux=localhost) and ci@petit aarch64-darwin (/tmp/olai-odu-petit.lock, --host aarch64-darwin=ci@petit) — the --host pin is mandatory (bare --platform dials dead kolu-ci boxes from hosts.json). For olai PRs EITHER platform green is the bar; kolu PRs need both. RULED 12:03 (human): olai's GitHub ruleset still requires the nine @x86_64-linux contexts — ADMIN MERGES ARE FINE for a macOS-only-green olai PR (`gh pr merge --squash --admin`); the ruleset is not narrowed. Measurements under the localhost flock. Brief: briefs/ci-venue-change.md.","odu-venue-update":"RULED by the human 2026-08-24 13:45: CI uses LOCALHOST as the Linux host until further instructions — kolu-ci-* being back changes nothing yet. The standing recipe stays: x86_64-linux on localhost under /tmp/olai-odu-localhost.lock with --host x86_64-linux=localhost; ci@petit aarch64-darwin under its flock when a darwin leg is wanted; either platform green is the bar for olai PRs","verification-2026-08-21":"production kolu#2194 FULL TEST with a real agent (c01109d6, 21:28–21:35) — ALL STAGES PASSED: spawn+boot; typed prompt + Enter; READY 42 in 1s; settle → test watch (--held-for 10s) transition at +10s arriving instantly (per-line flush VERIFIED); nag re-ring at exactly +45s and +90s; main watch (--held-for 60s) transition at +60s; second prompt → second transition; screen_text, kolu ls, --ignore mute list, --ignore-self, --heartbeat; loud death + re-arm twice; kill → terminal gone, state-knob watch silent by design (no gone event, per the contract). Orchestrator's verdict on #2194: GOOD — every claim exercised live on the production build; merge-ready from the consumer's seat.","watch-task":"RE-ARMED 2026-08-24 ~15:35 on the human's word after the orchestrator's process restart killed bowney4oj (which itself replaced b5o3nevw7 and bn865br9z across earlier restarts): Monitor task bmsrte0cx, kolu watch --states waiting,awaiting --held-for 60s --nag 10m, persistent, fleet-wide. Zero orchestrator lanes live at arming — the watch stands ready for the next dispatch. Find this node by prop:mute-list"}}
{"id":"experiment-kimi-k3","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a5","title":"Experiment (the human's, 2026-08-23): opencode + kimi-k3 as an implementing agent vs Claude Opus — observe only, compare at the end","doing":true,"created":"2026-08-23T09:27:02-04:00","changed":"2026-08-23T13:13:10-04:00","custom":{"baseline":"Claude Opus[1m] on lane-scli PR 1 (kolu#2205 @kolu/surface-cli): dispatched 16:09, PR open by 17:56 (1h47m), merged 22:10 (6h01m wall incl. kolu's /be gauntlet + two CI platforms + a redeploy stall ~8 min + an orchestrator venue ruling); 31 commits; 0 human interventions, 3 orchestrator rulings (venue ×2, /be process); 1 e2e flake rerun; 0 stop-and-asks. PR 2 (olai) in flight — its numbers will be added.","criteria":"wall-clock to first PR / to green / to merge; commits; human prompts answered (awaiting events); orchestrator/human rulings needed; review findings (must/should/nits) and how many rounds; CI reruns; context used at the end; scope honesty (deferrals, claims vs verified); tool friction (e.g. `pnpm: command not found` outside nix develop at 09:24)","observations":"09:22 first seen awaiting a 4-option prompt (the human answered); 09:24 working (pnpm outside the dev shell → not found → nix develop); context 111K. 09:57 still reading types, branch kolu-surface-face, context 195.9K (77%). 10:27 committing, context 90.7K (compacted/new session). 10:52 kolu#2206 \"Mount `kolu surface` — the agent API as shell verbs\" OPEN (≤1h30m from first sighting; Opus's first PR: 1h47m). 13:12 REPORTED DONE to the human: 5 commits, +1478/−161, draft; lanes it ran: kolu-mcp 85/85, kolu-cli 134/134, surface-cli 52/52, ci::unit 121, ci::daemon 363, just check + fmt, atlas rebuilt; GitHub Actions all green; evidence screenshot of the branch binary driving the production padi. Two honesty notes it volunteered: evidence captured locally not on a pu box; the full ci::default (Playwright e2e) NOT run — \"the odu MCP wasn't wired here\", only scoped lanes. No odu ci:: statuses posted at all (only GitHub's own checks) — so the PR has NOT been through kolu's /ci; its e2e is untested. Wall-clock 09:22→13:12 = 3h50m to a self-declared done without CI; context 187.7K at the end. Human prompts answered: ≥1 (09:22), plus whatever the human typed directly.","pr":"kolu#2206 \"Mount `kolu surface` — the agent API as shell verbs\" (branch kolu-surface-face) — open by 10:52, i.e. ≤1h30m after first seen (09:22); the Opus baseline's first PR took 1h47m from dispatch","task":"as seen 09:24: prototyping `kolu surface <verb>` in packages/kolu-cli on top of @kolu/surface-cli (proto-surface.ts; Command.make('surface') with the padi's verbs) — the kolu-cli migration #2205 explicitly left out","terminal":"bd0a0a9d-c9a8-4ed5-87b8-b29df90e0650 (opencode, model kimi-k3 'Build' agent), kolu worktree kolu-surface-cli — the HUMAN drives it; the orchestrator NEVER sends input, only reads"}}
